# MentorMates Project Rules

## Project Overview
This is a Next.js 15 TypeScript application called "MentorMates" - a mentorship and event management platform with project submission, feedback, and event management features.

## Tech Stack & Architecture
- **Framework**: Next.js 15 with App Router
- **Language**: TypeScript
- **Database**: Supabase (PostgreSQL)
- **Styling**: Tailwind CSS
- **UI Components**: Radix UI with shadcn/ui
- **Email**: Resend API + Nodemailer (Gmail)
- **Payment**: Stripe
- **Authentication**: Supabase Auth
- **State Management**: React Hook Form with Zod validation

## Project Structure
- **Feature-based architecture** in `features/` directory
- **App Router** with API routes in `app/api/`
- **Shared components** in `components/`
- **Utilities** in `lib/`
- **Email templates** in `lib/email_templates/`

## Code Style & Standards

### File Naming
- Use kebab-case for files and directories
- Use PascalCase for React components
- Use camelCase for functions and variables

### Component Structure
- Prefer function components with TypeScript
- Use proper TypeScript interfaces/types
- Follow the existing component patterns in `components/ui/`
- Use Radix UI components via shadcn/ui

### API Routes
- Follow REST conventions
- Use proper HTTP status codes
- Include error handling with try-catch
- Validate inputs with Zod schemas
- Use Supabase client for database operations

### Email System
- Email types defined in `lib/email_templates/constants.ts`
- Templates in `lib/email_templates/` directory
- Two email providers: Resend (notifications) and Nodemailer (project emails)
- Email endpoints:
  - `/api/email` - Project submission and feedback emails
  - `/api/email_notification/event/[eventId]` - Event notifications
  - `/api/email_notification/user/[userId]` - User-specific notifications

### Database Patterns
- Use Supabase client from `@/app/utils/supabase/server`
- Follow RLS (Row Level Security) patterns
- Use proper error handling for database operations

### Styling
- Use Tailwind CSS utility classes
- Follow the existing design system
- Use CSS variables for theming (light/dark mode support)
- Prefer Tailwind over custom CSS

## Development Guidelines

### Import Statements
- Use absolute imports with `@/` prefix
- Group imports: React/Next, third-party, local components, types
- Use proper TypeScript imports for types

### Error Handling
- Always handle errors in API routes
- Use proper HTTP status codes (400, 401, 404, 500)
- Provide meaningful error messages
- Log errors for debugging

### Security
- Validate all inputs
- Use Supabase RLS for data access control
- Sanitize user inputs
- Use environment variables for sensitive data

### Performance
- Use Next.js Image component for images
- Implement proper loading states
- Use React.memo for expensive components
- Optimize database queries

## Email System Details

### Email Types
- `EVENT_UPDATE` - General event updates
- `EVENT_SCHEDULE_UPDATE` - Schedule changes
- `EVENT_CUSTOM_UPDATE` - Custom notifications
- `CHECKIN_QR_CODE` - Check-in tickets

### Email Templates
- Project submission confirmations
- Teammate notifications
- Feedback notifications
- Event updates and notifications
- QR code tickets

### Email Configuration
- Resend API for event notifications (`NOTIFICATIONS_EMAIL_FROM`)
- Gmail SMTP for project-related emails
- Environment variables: `RESEND_API_KEY`, `EMAIL_USER`, `EMAIL_APP_PASSWORD`

## Specific Patterns

### Form Handling
- Use React Hook Form with Zod validation
- Create reusable form components
- Handle loading and error states properly

### Data Fetching
- Use Supabase client for server-side operations
- Implement proper error boundaries
- Use loading states and error handling

### Authentication
- Use Supabase Auth
- Check user authentication in API routes
- Implement proper role-based access control

## Best Practices
- Write clean, readable TypeScript code
- Use meaningful variable and function names
- Comment complex logic
- Follow the existing patterns in the codebase
- Test edge cases and error conditions
- Keep components focused and reusable
- Use proper semantic HTML
- Ensure accessibility standards

## When Working on This Project
- Always check existing patterns before creating new ones
- Use the established component library (shadcn/ui + Radix)
- Follow the feature-based architecture
- Maintain consistency with existing code style
- Update types when changing data structures
- Test email functionality in development
- Ensure responsive design for all components